they were the subjects of the so-called  tinker experiment  they call it eugenics social engineering  over decades  that separated families and ruined lives  i was born in an experiment  and had no say anymore  in a clearing in a pursue forest is the  gypsy traveller community  seamus mcphee was born into 50 years ago  then it was one location of many for the  tinker experiment  primitive hearts seen here after they  were occupied  built to encourage gypsy travelers away  from a nomadic existence  and towards settle society but all  executed  with sinister intent according to  shameless  to demolish and eradicate gypsy culture  and to affect a form of cultural  genocide  and it was part of a punitive series of  measures  you know a drive against offseason  purges against gypsy travelers  with a view to making them conform  the tinker experiment led to some  families being broken up  if a family outgrew the accommodation it  was given  children could be taken into care the  damage is done  it won't be repaired teresa was one of  those children  even before she and her twin brother  were born they were earmarked for  removal from the family home  her brother died in middle age an  alcoholic  teresa blames a lifelong trauma rooted  in his childhood experience  it had a terrible impact on his life  he's the one that suffered the most  because he couldn't cope with it  there were several thousand people  involved in the so-called tinker  experiments  which lasted over many years in recent  years  those involved have sought a formal  apology from the scottish government  which hasn't been forthcoming a  spokesperson said  we accept the lives of many gypsy  travelers have been blighted by  historical policies and practices  of councils and charities and we  absolutely recognize the devastating  and lasting impact this had we must now  focus on working together  to deliver the actions to address the  inequality and injustice  that this community continues to face  it's a government's stated intention to  get things right  if not the apology sought for an  experiment gone wrong  james matthews sky news in perthshire
 

